	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Setup

Enable Logseq's HTTP API server (Settings → Features), paste its token into Configure Workflow, and keep the DB graph open. For files and pictures, install the Logseq Plugin (0.3.25 or newer) in Logseq.

## Ways in

- `{var:today_keyword} words` — a bullet on today's journal.
- `{var:active_keyword} words` — a bullet on the page open in Logseq.
- `{var:page_keyword} Name` — a page named so, made if there is none; end with `#Tag` to tag it with an existing tag.
- `{var:picture_keyword}` — the picture on the clipboard, into the graph on today's journal; `{var:picture_keyword} Name` puts it on a page named so.
- **Add to Logseq Today** (Universal Action, or the hotkey) — files into the graph on today's journal; selected words as a quote with a citation to where they came from; a web page as its link.
- **Add to Logseq as a page** (Universal Action) — the same, each on a page of its own: a file on a page named after it, words on a page named after the page they came from.

A file put into the graph is a node of its own, as when it is dropped into Logseq: the plugin's Cite finds a PDF, Threads lists it, and it opens inside Logseq.</string>
